    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30215" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mycŏnos</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-us</span></b> , i, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μύκονος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one of the Cyctades</i>, now <i>Mykoni</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 7,
				11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 3, 76</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 7,
				463</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mycŏnĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Myconos, Myconian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					14, 7, 9, § 75</span></i>
			.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mycŏnĭi</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Myconos, the Myconians</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 11,
				37, 47, § 130</span></i>.</div>
